# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/festivals.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event starfall_jars
# en: Star Jars
title [b671d5] = 星罐
# en: {The Stargazers have set up tables under the dome, and everyone is making a jar to catch a falling star in tonight. Nobody has caught one in years. Everyone tries.|The jar tables are out under the dome again, and the first-years are making theirs all wrong.|Star jars again. You know which glass holds and which cracks in the cold.} {~The Stargazers are arguing about the forecast.|Somebody has painted a jar entirely gold.|The telescope keeps swinging toward the lake.}
text [e99045] = {观星社在穹顶下摆好了桌子，每个人都在做一只罐子，好在今晚接住一颗坠落的星星。好些年没人接住过了。人人都还是要试。|罐子桌又摆到了穹顶下，一年级生们的罐子全做错了。|又是星罐。哪种玻璃经得住寒气、哪种会裂，你已经心里有数了。} {~观星社的人在争论天气预报。|有人把一只罐子整个涂成了金色。|望远镜总是往湖的方向转。}
# en: Long trestle tables under the observatory dome covered in glass jars, students painting stars on them, one of the Stargazers handing out corks.
scene [04d125] = 观星台穹顶下的长条桌上摆满了玻璃罐，学生们在上面画星星，一位观星社的社员在分发软木塞。
# en: Make a proper jar
opt.left.label [2c03ab] = 做一只像样的罐子
# en: {~Thick glass, a cork sealed with wax, a rune for luck scratched into the lid. "Better odds tonight," says one of the Stargazers. "Theoretically."|You buy the good glass and take your time over it. It's the best jar on the table, and you know it.}
opt.left.say.1 [92d651] = {~厚玻璃，用蜡封的软木塞，盖子上刻一道祈求好运的符文。“今晚的胜算更大了，”一位观星社的社员说。“理论上。”|你买了好玻璃，慢慢地做。这是桌上最好的一只罐子，你自己也知道。}
# en: Help the Stargazers set up the roof
opt.right.label [7691a1] = 帮观星社布置屋顶
# en: {~You haul blankets and telescopes up the observatory stairs all afternoon. Your arms ache. The Stargazers save you the best spot on the roof.|Blankets, cushions, a kettle that has to be carried up four hundred steps. The Stargazers know your name by the end of it.}
opt.right.say.1 [7694e2] = {~你一下午都在把毯子和望远镜往观星台的楼梯上搬。胳膊酸疼。观星社给你留了屋顶上最好的位置。|毯子、坐垫，还有一只得扛着爬四百级台阶的水壶。到最后，观星社的人都记住了你的名字。}

@event starfall_together
# en: A Blanket for Two
title [7474ae] = 两人一条毯子
# en: You find {partner} on the lawn below the observatory with a blanket already spread for two and a flask of something hot. "I saved you the sky," {they} say{s}. The first star falls before you've sat down.
text [894c38] = 你在观星台下的草坪上找到了 {partner}，毯子已经为两个人铺好了，还带着一壶热乎乎的东西。“我给你留了一片天空，”{they} 说。你还没坐下，第一颗星星就落了下来。
# en: Two students lying on a blanket on the lawn at night, wrapped in one shawl, a falling star streaking over the castle towers.
scene [cd2222] = 夜晚的草坪上，两个学生裹着同一条披肩躺在毯子上，一颗流星划过城堡的塔楼。
# en: Stay out until dawn
opt.left.label [b0f836] = 在外面待到天亮
# en: You stay out until the sky turns grey, counting stars and then not counting anything. You're both frozen and hoarse and late for breakfast, and it was worth all of it.
opt.left.say.1 [ce070c] = 你们一直待到天色发灰，先是数星星，后来什么也不数了。你们俩都冻僵了，嗓子也哑了，早饭也迟到了，而这一切都值得。
# en: Tell {them} what you wished for
opt.right.label [28c1f2] = 告诉 {them} 你许了什么愿
# en: You say it out loud, which you're told ruins a wish. {partner} goes very quiet and then tells you {their} own. Neither of you minds if it's ruined.
opt.right.say.1 [069e3e] = 你把它说出了口，据说这样愿望就不灵了。{partner} 安静了很久，然后也告诉了你 {their}愿望。你们俩都不在乎它灵不灵了。

@event starfall_wish
# en: A Wish on a Falling Star
title [a426d8] = 向流星许愿
# en: The oldest Starfall custom: pick one star, the brightest you'll see all night, and give it one wish. The Stargazers say a wish you spend on someone else falls slower. Nobody knows what that means. A very bright one is coming down over the lake.
text [c2e706] = 星坠节最古老的习俗：挑一颗星，这一夜你能看到的最亮的那颗，把一个愿望交给它。观星社的人说，为别人许的愿，星星会落得慢一些。没人知道这是什么意思。一颗非常亮的星正朝湖面落下。
# en: A student kneeling on the observatory roof with eyes closed, hands clasped, a bright star falling over the dark lake below.
scene [ba4b65] = 一个学生跪在观星台屋顶上，闭着眼睛，双手合十，一颗明亮的星星正落向下方漆黑的湖面。
# en: Wish for your own year
opt.left.label [e770b9] = 为自己的这一年许愿
# en: You wish hard and selfishly, and the star burns out over the water. It feels like a promise you've made to yourself, which is heavier than you expected.
opt.left.say.1 [c2813c] = 你用力地、自私地许了愿，那颗星在水面上燃尽了。这感觉像是对自己许下的承诺，比你想象的要沉。
# en: Wish for someone else
opt.right.label [bc6686] = 为别人许愿
# en: You don't say who. The star falls slowly, or you imagine it does, all the way down to the lake.
opt.right.say.1 [7dd3ec] = 你没说是为谁。那颗星落得很慢，或者是你以为它很慢，一直落进了湖里。

@event starfall_caught
# en: The Star in the Jar
title [3b66bd] = 罐中之星
# en: The star you caught at Starfall still glows in its jar on your windowsill, a little dimmer each night. A collector in the village has offered good money for it. One of the Stargazers says it would like to go back up, if stars like anything.
text [f775be] = 你在星坠节接住的那颗星，还在窗台上的罐子里发着光，一夜比一夜暗一点。村里有位收藏家出了个好价钱。一位观星社的社员说，如果星星也会想要什么的话，它想回到天上去。
# en: A glass jar on a dormitory windowsill holding a tiny glowing star, a pale light on the curtains, frost on the outside of the glass.
scene [c5924e] = 宿舍窗台上的一只玻璃罐里装着一颗发光的小星星，窗帘上映着淡淡的光，玻璃外结了霜。
# en: Keep it by your bed
opt.keep.label [b48f7a] = 把它放在床边
# en: You keep it, and buy oil to keep the window frost off it. It fades by spring, slowly, like a coal. The last night it glows, you sit up with it.
opt.keep.say.1 [fb1cf4] = 你留下了它，还买了灯油来防止窗户结霜。它到春天才慢慢熄灭，像一块炭。它发光的最后一夜，你一直陪着它。
# en: Sell it to the collector
opt.sell.label [90e67f] = 卖给收藏家
# en: The collector holds it up to the light and pays without haggling. The windowsill looks very dark that night.
opt.sell.say.1 [30c842] = 收藏家把它举到灯下，一分没还价就付了钱。那天晚上，窗台显得格外暗。
# en: Let it go from the roof
opt.release.label [6abecc] = 从屋顶放它走
# en: You climb the observatory at midnight and open the jar. It hangs there a moment, then rises, slow and sure, until you can't tell it from the others. A few people saw. The story goes round by breakfast.
opt.release.say.1 [233362] = 你半夜爬上观星台，打开了罐子。它在那儿悬停了片刻，然后缓缓地、坚定地升起，直到你再也分不清它和其他星星。有几个人看见了。到早饭时，这个故事已经传开了。

@event starfall_at_home
# en: Starfall at Home
title [e21d08] = 家中的星坠节
# en: {Starfall at home. There's no observatory here, only the cottage roof and the whole family on it in quilts, as when you were small.|Starfall at home again. Someone has saved you the warm patch of roof by the chimney.|The roof, the quilts, the chimney. Someone asks what the academy does for Starfall, and you find you'd rather be here.} {~The village dogs howl at every star.|Somebody's brought cocoa.|A neighbour is telling the one about the star that fell in the duck pond.}
text [a3f4a7] = {家里的星坠节。这里没有观星台，只有小屋的屋顶，全家人裹着被子坐在上面，就像你小时候那样。|又是在家过星坠节。有人给你留了烟囱旁那块暖和的屋顶。|屋顶、被子、烟囱。有人问学院里怎么过星坠节，你发现自己更愿意待在这儿。} {~村里的狗冲着每一颗星星嚎叫。|有人带了热可可。|一位邻居在讲那颗星星掉进鸭塘的老故事。}
# en: A family on the roof of a cottage at night, wrapped in quilts, a small child pointing at a streak of light across the sky.
scene [02170e] = 夜里，一家人裹着被子坐在小屋的屋顶上，一个小孩指着划过天空的一道光。
# en: Tell them about the academy
opt.left.label [e245d0] = 给他们讲学院的事
# en: {~You tell them about the towers and the lake and the staircase that moves, and they ask questions until the stars run out. It's past three when you climb down, cold to the bone and glad.|Everyone wants a story. You give them the best ones, slightly improved. Nobody minds.}
opt.left.say.1 [10eafc] = {~你给他们讲塔楼、湖，还有会移动的楼梯，他们一直问到星星落完。你爬下屋顶时已经过了三点，冻透了，心里却很高兴。|每个人都想听故事。你把最好的那些讲给他们听，稍微润色了一下。没人介意。}
# en: Slip off to the hill alone
opt.right.label [1f9874] = 独自溜到山坡上
# en: {~From the hill behind the cottage you name every star the way they taught you, and a few the way you learned as a child. Both names are right.|Alone on the hill, you watch the sky the way an academy student does now, and miss, a little, the way you used to.}
opt.right.say.1 [35c67a] = {~在小屋后面的山坡上，你按学院教的方法给每颗星星命名，又按小时候学的叫法叫了几颗。两个名字都对。|你独自在山坡上，用学院学生的眼光看着天空，有一点怀念从前看天的样子。}

@event starfall_on_internship
# en: Starfall Far From Home
title [c56ee2] = 远离家乡的星坠节
# en: Starfall, and you're far from the observatory roof. {member(intern_expedition): Up at the ridge camp the sky is enormous, and the expedition's astronomers are working through it, counting every streak.|{member(intern_thornwick): Thornwick marks Starfall with illusions, and the lawn is full of false stars falling among the real ones. {met(tamsin): Tamsin finds you and points out which ones are theirs.|}|{member(intern_field_station): At the field station the creatures are restless under the falling stars, and someone has to sit up with them.|{member(intern_royal_library) or member(intern_unseen_office): The city has no lawns, only rooftops, and every one of them has people on it tonight.|The other interns have found a flat roof and a crate of something fizzy, and your supervisor is pretending not to know.}}}}
text [daf3a0] = 星坠节，而你离观星台的屋顶很远。{member(intern_expedition): 山脊营地上的天空无比辽阔，考察队的天文学家们正在一颗颗地记录，每一道流光都不放过。|{member(intern_thornwick): 荆木学院用幻术庆祝星坠节，草坪上假的星星和真的星星一起坠落。{met(tamsin): 塔姆辛找到了你，指给你看哪些是 TA 做的。|}|{member(intern_field_station): 在野外观测站，动物们在坠落的星光下躁动不安，总得有人守着它们。|{member(intern_royal_library) or member(intern_unseen_office): 城里没有草坪，只有屋顶，而今晚每一片屋顶上都有人。|其他实习生找到了一片平屋顶和一箱冒泡的饮料，你的导师假装不知道。}}}}
# en: A group of interns on a flat roof far from the academy, wrapped in coats, watching falling stars over unfamiliar rooftops.
scene [2a4dd5] = 远离学院的一片平屋顶上，一群实习生裹着外套，看着陌生屋顶上空坠落的星星。
# en: Join the others on the roof
opt.left.label [a3d8dd] = 和其他人一起上屋顶
# en: {~You lie on a strange roof among people you met two months ago and count stars until they feel like old friends. Tomorrow's work goes slowly.|Coats, a borrowed blanket, someone's terrible song. It's not the observatory roof, and it's good anyway.}
opt.left.say.1 [a34087] = {~你躺在一片陌生的屋顶上，身边是两个月前才认识的人，数星星数到他们仿佛成了老朋友。第二天的工作进展很慢。|外套、借来的毯子、某人糟糕透顶的歌。这不是观星台的屋顶，但也很好。}
# en: Keep working through the night
opt.right.label [8ae9d3] = 通宵工作
# en: {~You work through it with the window open, glancing up now and then. Your supervisor finds the finished work on the desk at dawn and raises an eyebrow, which is a great deal from them.|The stars fall outside while you finish the job. You see a few. Your supervisor sees all of it.}
opt.right.say.1 [88a708] = {~你开着窗工作了一整夜，时不时抬头看一眼。导师在黎明时发现桌上完成的工作，扬了扬眉毛，对他们来说这已经是很高的评价了。|星星在窗外坠落，你在屋里把活干完。你看到了几颗。你的导师看到了全部。}

@event ball_robes
# en: Something to Wear
title [d096f3] = 穿什么好
# en: {year == 1: The Midwinter Ball is tonight, and you have nothing to wear that isn't a uniform or a nightshirt.|{final_year: The last ball of your life as a student. The old robes look very tired.|{~Ball night again, and last year's robes have shrunk, somehow, in the trunk.|Ball night again. Your robes have a stain on the cuff you'd forgotten about.}}} {~The village tailor is open till three.|Your roommate is already dressed and gloating.|The mirror has opinions.}
text [70f547] = {year == 1: 仲冬舞会就在今晚，而你除了校服和睡衣，什么能穿的都没有。|{final_year: 你学生时代的最后一场舞会。旧礼袍看起来疲惫极了。|{~又到舞会之夜，去年的礼袍不知怎么在箱子里缩水了。|又到舞会之夜。你的礼袍袖口上有块你早忘了的污渍。}}} {~村里的裁缝铺开到三点。|你的室友已经穿戴整齐，正在得意。|镜子有自己的看法。}
# en: A dormitory room strewn with robes, a student holding up a moth-eaten formal robe against themselves before a cracked mirror.
scene [e36b69] = 宿舍里散落着各式礼袍，一个学生站在裂了缝的镜子前，把一件被虫蛀过的礼袍比在身上。
# en: Buy new robes in the village
opt.left.label [b6ca12] = 去村里买新礼袍
# en: {~Deep blue, with a lining like the night sky. In the tailor's mirror you look, for once, like someone in a portrait.|New robes, a sensible colour and an insensible price. They fit as if they were waiting for you.}
opt.left.say.1 [b6968c] = {~深蓝色，衬里像夜空。在裁缝铺的镜子里，你难得一次看起来像画像里的人。|新礼袍，颜色稳重，价格不稳重。合身得像是一直在等你。}
# en: Glamour your old ones
opt.right.label [f20065] = 给旧礼袍施个幻术
# en: The old robes shimmer into silk. Nobody guesses, and three people ask where you had them made.
opt.right.say.1 [3d5149] = 旧礼袍闪烁着变成了丝绸。没人看出来，还有三个人问你是在哪儿做的。
# en: At the stroke of nine your glamour slips, and the mended elbow shows through the silk like a confession. You keep your arm by your side all night.
opt.right.say.2 [76df3a] = 九点钟一到，你的幻术失效了，补过的手肘透过丝绸露了出来，像一份供词。你整晚都把胳膊贴在身侧。

@event ball_ice_garden
# en: The Ice Garden
title [ed8110] = 冰之花园
# en: {The frost-mages have turned the courtyard into an ice garden for the ball. Frozen roses line the paths, and the fountain has stopped mid-splash.|The ice garden again, bigger this year, with a hedge maze of frost.|The ice garden, and you know its paths by heart now.} {~Couples are walking it before the music has started.|A first-year has got their tongue stuck to a rose.|The lanterns make the ice glow blue.}
text [4d5a77] = {霜法师们把庭院变成了一座迎接舞会的冰之花园。冰冻的玫瑰排列在小径两旁，喷泉停在了水花溅起的那一刻。|又是冰之花园，今年更大了，还有一座霜做的树篱迷宫。|冰之花园，你现在已经熟悉它的每一条小径了。} {~音乐还没响起，情侣们已经在里面漫步了。|一个一年级生的舌头粘在了一朵玫瑰上。|灯笼让冰透出蓝光。}
# en: A castle courtyard turned into a garden of ice, frozen roses along glittering paths, a fountain stopped mid-splash, students walking under lanterns.
scene [47b745] = 城堡庭院变成了一座冰的花园，闪光的小径旁是冰冻的玫瑰，喷泉停在水花溅起的一刻，学生们在灯笼下漫步。
# en: Walk it slowly
opt.left.label [3e196d] = 慢慢地逛
# en: {~You walk every path twice, until your toes are numb and your head is clear. The fountain's frozen spray catches the light like a held breath.|You find the centre of the maze, where someone has left a frozen bench and a frozen apple. You sit a while.}
opt.left.say.1 [ce3c18] = {~每条小径你都走了两遍，直到脚趾冻麻、脑袋清醒。喷泉冻住的水花映着光，像一口屏住的呼吸。|你找到了迷宫的中心，那里有人留下了一张冰冻的长椅和一个冰冻的苹果。你坐了一会儿。}
# en: Help the frost-mages finish it
opt.right.label [946705] = 帮霜法师们收尾
# en: {~They show you how to hold the cold in a petal until it sets. Your hands ache for an hour. One of the roses on the path is yours.|You shape a whole archway of ice under instruction, and it holds. The frost-mages nod, which is how they applaud.}
opt.right.say.1 [414e46] = {~他们教你怎么把寒气留在花瓣里直到它定形。你的手疼了一个小时。小径上有一朵玫瑰是你做的。|你在指导下塑出了一整座冰拱门，而且它立住了。霜法师们点了点头，他们就是这样鼓掌的。}

@event ball_last_dance
# en: The Last Waltz
title [686d0e] = 最后一支华尔兹
# en: Near midnight the musicians play the last waltz, slow and a little sad. {npc} holds out a hand without saying anything. Half the hall has gone to bed. The chandelier is dripping.
text [ddb155] = 快到午夜时，乐师们奏起了最后一支华尔兹，缓慢，带着一点忧伤。{npc} 一言不发地伸出手。大厅里一半的人已经去睡了。枝形吊灯在滴水。
# en: The great hall near midnight, candles burning low, a single couple still turning slowly beneath a dripping ice-crystal chandelier.
scene [cf17c9] = 将近午夜的大礼堂，蜡烛快要燃尽，一盏滴着水的冰晶吊灯下，只剩一对舞伴还在缓缓旋转。
# en: Dance until the music stops
opt.left.label [bf83ad] = 一直跳到音乐停止
# en: You dance it slowly, and then once more after the musicians have packed up, to no music at all. Nobody else is left to see, which is the point.
opt.left.say.1 [7c3db6] = 你们慢慢地跳完这一支，然后在乐师们收拾好乐器之后，在没有音乐的寂静里又跳了一遍。没有别人留下来看，这正是重点。
# en: Slip out onto the frozen terrace
opt.right.label [50e9ea] = 溜到结冰的露台上
# en: Outside it's bitter, and the stars are out over the lake. You talk until you can't feel your fingers, about nothing and then about everything, and go back in blue-lipped and grinning.
opt.right.say.1 [dfa865] = 外面冷得刺骨，湖面上空满是星星。你们一直聊到手指失去知觉，先聊无关紧要的事，后来聊了一切，回去时嘴唇发紫，笑得合不拢嘴。

@event ball_snowball_war
# en: The Snowball War
title [da2e94] = 雪仗
# en: {After the ball, someone throws the first snowball in the courtyard, and within a minute every house is at war, in ball robes.|The snowball war, as much a tradition as the ball. The forts went up during the last waltz.|The snowball war again. The first-years have built a fort that is frankly impressive.} {~A prefect is trying to restore order and failing.|Someone has enchanted their snowballs, which is cheating.|The robes are already ruined.}
text [26e610] = {舞会结束后，有人在庭院里扔出了第一个雪球，不到一分钟，各学院就穿着舞会礼服打成了一片。|雪仗，和舞会一样是传统。雪堡是在最后一支华尔兹时堆起来的。|又是雪仗。一年级生们堆的雪堡坦白说相当壮观。} {~一位级长想恢复秩序，没成功。|有人给自己的雪球施了魔法，这是作弊。|礼服早就毁了。}
# en: A snowy courtyard at night full of students in ruined ball robes hurling snowballs from behind snow forts, a prefect ducking.
scene [733bb8] = 夜晚积雪的庭院里，一群穿着破烂舞会礼服的学生躲在雪堡后面互扔雪球，一位级长正在闪躲。
# en: Charge the enemy fort
opt.left.label [f5a047] = 冲向敌方雪堡
# en: You take the fort with a war cry and a single perfect throw. Your house carries you round the fountain on its shoulders. Your robes will never recover.
opt.left.say.1 [0b4ca7] = 你一声战吼加一记完美的投掷，攻下了雪堡。你的学院把你扛在肩上绕着喷泉转圈。你的礼服再也恢复不了了。
# en: A snowball, then fourteen. You go down laughing under a drift, and someone has to dig you out. Worth it.
opt.left.say.2 [ff0315] = 一个雪球，然后是十四个。你笑着被埋进了雪堆，还得有人把你挖出来。值了。
# en: Watch from the cloister with cocoa
opt.right.label [6ac2a1] = 端着可可在回廊里看
# en: {~You watch from the cloister, warm and dry, and cheer for whoever's losing. Nobody throws at you. Mostly.|You hold the cocoa and the coats, and you're the only one who goes to bed warm.}
opt.right.say.1 [19a22b] = {~你在回廊里看着，温暖又干燥，为输的那一方加油。没人朝你扔雪球。大多数时候。|你替大家拿着可可和外套，是唯一一个暖暖和和上床睡觉的人。}
